WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.675
Before comparing anything, the pipeline
makes sure the comparison means something.

2
00:00:04.675 --> 00:00:07.929
It checks each run against
the kit's own manifest,

3
00:00:07.929 --> 00:00:10.613
so a run edited after the fact is refused.

4
00:00:10.613 --> 00:00:15.725
Then it refuses to compare runs from
different modes or clouds, or out of order.

5
00:00:15.725 --> 00:00:17.359
The subtle one is tenants:

6
00:00:17.359 --> 00:00:21.250
a test tenant and production can
share a cloud and look alike.

7
00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:24.295
The kit records the tenant
the token was issued for,

8
00:00:24.295 --> 00:00:28.572
and the pipeline refuses to compare
two different tenants, or a run with

9
00:00:28.572 --> 00:00:32.900
no tenant recorded at all, unless
someone records a reviewed exception.
